{"id":"65b6be2b4bac2474b2dfa5639fcd5f780f5356a9","axis":"silent","repo":"QwikDev/qwik","sha":"65b6be2b4bac2474b2dfa5639fcd5f780f5356a9","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/core-qrls-library-mode.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+'@qwik.dev/core': patch","+---","+","+refactor: core's own QRLs compile like any Qwik library's"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":".ruler/skills/qwik-core-development/references/core-notes.md","lines":["@@ -238,19 +238,19 @@ Out-of-order (OOOS) invariants:","   variant at another with an `export *` stub: the self-import cycles through the stub. Terser runs per","   chunk, so its mangled names must not end in `$` (optimizers read `x$()` as a marker) and mangled","   `$props$` must avoid plain property names of every chunk, not just the one being minified.","-- Core's own QRLs (event wrapper, bind handlers, visible tasks, control flow, HMR, eager resume) are","-  `_inlinedQrl(fn, 'q_<hash>', [captures])` calls, with `inlinedQrl as _inlinedQrl` imported from","-  `shared/qrl/library-qrl.ts`; the build turns that import into `@qwik.dev/core`. Never create them","-  with `createQRL(null, '_x', fn)`: the optimizer must see them to give them a chunk and a dev URL.","-  Add each hash to `CORE_QRL_HASHES` and match core QRLs by hash, not symbol (prod renames `q_run`","-  to `s_run`). Pass `fn` as a function declaration (the Rust optimizer's SSR output calls `.s(fn)`","-  at the top of the module) or, so the segment owns the code, as an inline named function","-  expression that reads only module scope and `_capturesObj`; never as a `const` arrow. Give the","-  QRL a name different from `fn`'s, or dev segments redeclare it.","-- Only event/task handler QRLs share the app's `qwik-core` chunk (the `qwik-core` group in","-  `packages/qwik-vite/src/plugins/plugin.ts` lists their hashes). Everything else, like the","-  control-flow components, is an ordinary segment: write its function inline at the QRL site and","-  don't export it, or the segment is a one-line re-export and its code stays in every app's core.","+- Write core's own QRLs with `$()`, `component$()` and `useTask$()` imported from their relative","+  modules. `scripts/core-library-qrls.ts` compiles them in library mode, for core's build and for","+  the unit tests (`vitest.config.ts`), so each app's optimizer extracts them like any library's. A","+  `foo$` marker needs `fooQrl` exported from the same module: the optimizer imports it from there.","+  In the unit tests core's modules load unbundled, so a QRL created at the top level of a module","+  that `qrl-class.ts` imports transitively runs before `createQRL` exists: create it on first use.","+- Functions that read their own captures (the qwikloader calls them with the captures as `this`)","+  get their QRLs in `shared/qrl/handler-qrls.ts`, bound with `.w(captures)`. Import them there","+  through `core-handlers.ts`: its file name prefixes their segment names, which the `qwik-core`","+  group in `packages/qwik-vite/src/plugins/plugin.ts` keeps in core's chunk, so a cold click doesn't","+  spend a round trip on `_run` before it knows its handler. Core itself has no special preload: it's","+  a static import in the bundle graph like any chunk. Write every other QRL, like the control-flow","+  components', inline at its `$()` site, so its segment owns the code."," "," ## Focused Verification"," "],"additions":13,"deletions":13,"truncated":false},{"path":"e2e/qwik-e2e/apps/qwikrouter-ssg-snapshot/expected.ssg.html","lines":["@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@","-<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"en\" q:render=\"static-ssr\" q:route=\"/\" q:container=\"paused\" q:runtime=\"2\" q:base=\"/build/\" q:locale=\"\" q:manifest-hash=\"MANIFEST_HASH\" q:instance=\"[instance]\" :><head :><link rel=\"modulepreload\" href=\"/build/q-xxxxxxxx.js\" :><script type=\"text/javascript\">import(new URL(\"/build/q-xxxxxxxx.js\",document.baseURI).href)</script><link rel=\"modulepreload\" href=\"/build/q-xxxxxxxx.js\" :>